<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $8.9 mln March 12.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $8.9 mln March 12.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $8.9 million deficit on March 12 in the commercial forex market, according to central bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MARCH 12</p>
<p>Exports: $190.1 million</p>
<p>Imports: $177.2 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $180 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $201.8 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $8.9 million</p>
<p>MARCH DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.677 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.365 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.895 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.411 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $796 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 2485415))</p>
